{"name":"Copper peptide scalp serum","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":59,"casual":{"lead":["Copper peptide scalp serums put GHK-Cu, a small copper-binding peptide found naturally in the body, on the scalp. Hair-loss communities add them to topical routines aiming for thicker hair and a denser hairline.","The idea draws on GHK-Cu's role in skin repair, supporting wound healing, collagen and blood vessel growth. Most GHK-Cu research is in cell and animal studies, with a few small, short facial-skin studies. No scalp hair-loss trials were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["It is used as a leave-on cosmetic serum on the scalp, typically added to a stack of other topical hair products. Users generally describe a routine of consistent use over months."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["It is sold as a cosmetic ingredient. The source notes GHK-Cu also raises matrix metalloproteinases and advises caution. Scalp-specific safety data are not available."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Safety and Efficacy of Approved and Unapproved Peptide Therapies for Musculoskeletal Injuries and Athletic Performance.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41966639/","source":"Sports medicine (Auckland, N.Z.)","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Injectable Peptide Therapy: A Primer for Orthopaedic and Sports Medicine Physicians.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41476424/","source":"The American journal of sports medicine","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Therapeutic Peptides in Orthopaedics: Applications, Challenges, and Future Directions.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41490200/","source":"Journal of the American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons. Global research & reviews","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Topically applied GHK as an anti-wrinkle peptide: Advantages, problems and prospective.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39963574/","source":"BioImpacts : BI","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Are We Ready to Measure Skin Permeation of Modern Antiaging GHK-Cu Tripeptide Encapsulated in Liposomes?","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39795193/","source":"Molecules (Basel, Switzerland)","year":2025,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"The potential of GHK as an anti-aging peptide.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35083444/","source":"Aging pathobiology and therapeutics","year":2020,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Regenerative and Protective Actions of the GHK-Cu Peptide in the Light of the New Gene Data.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29986520/","source":"International journal of molecular sciences","year":2018,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Effects of topical copper tripeptide complex on CO2 laser-resurfaced skin.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16847171/","source":"Archives of facial plastic surgery","year":2006,"cites":null,"kind":"Randomized Controlled Trial"}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"GHK-Cu Microneedling Use","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-microneedling-use.1855134/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260215174337/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-microneedling-use.1855134/"},{"title":"Ghk-Cu for skin?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-for-skin.1827238/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260202123208/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-for-skin.1827238/"},{"title":"Ghk-cu fountain","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-fountain.1820729/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260202162819/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-fountain.1820729/"},{"title":"ghk cu facial pinning","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-facial-pinning.1819870/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260305045602/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-facial-pinning.1819870/"},{"title":"ghk cu or retatt