ved":"https://web.archive.org/web/20241222174110/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-for-heightmaxxing.1215965/"},{"title":"ghk cu and the gene expressions it modulates and by what","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-and-the-gene-expressions-it-modulates-and-by-what.108661/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230224054947/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-and-the-gene-expressions-it-modulates-and-by-what.108661/"},{"title":"what should my doses be for ghk cu","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/what-should-my-doses-be-for-ghk-cu.1989641/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260407015831/https://looksmax.org/threads/what-should-my-doses-be-for-ghk-cu.1989641/"},{"title":"how much bac water for 100mg ghk cu","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-much-bac-water-for-100mg-ghk-cu.1817789/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260310124313/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-much-bac-water-for-100mg-ghk-cu.1817789/"},{"title":"sources for ghk cu 50mg indiamart","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/sources-for-ghk-cu-50mg-indiamart.1801840/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260103105359/https://looksmax.org/threads/sources-for-ghk-cu-50mg-indiamart.1801840/"},{"title":"topical ghk cu","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-ghk-cu.1790158/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228173222/https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-ghk-cu.1790158/"},{"title":"topical ghk cu","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-ghk-cu.1785128/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228072134/https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-ghk-cu.1785128/"},{"title":"effects of topical ghk cu and is it better than injecting","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/effects-of-topical-ghk-cu-and-is-it-better-than-injecting.1781894/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260215023335/https://looksmax.org/threads/effects-of-topical-ghk-cu-and-is-it-better-than-injecting.1781894/"},{"title":"how to inject ghk cu in face","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-inject-ghk-cu-in-face.1781396/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260116084642/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-to-inject-ghk-cu-in-face.1781396/"},{"title":"topical or subcuteneous ghk cu","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-or-subcuteneous-ghk-cu.1770815/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251220034653/https://looksmax.org/threads/topical-or-subcuteneous-ghk-cu.1770815/"},{"title":"how many days till ghk cu injection stop hurting","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/how-many-days-till-ghk-cu-injection-stop-hurting.1770547/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251230104010/https://looksmax.org/threads/how-many-days-till-ghk-cu-injection-stop-hurting.1770547/"},{"title":"will ghk cu 2 mg help with my hypertrophic acne scars","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/will-ghk-cu-2-mg-help-with-my-hypertrophic-acne-scars.1768636/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251217223905/https://looksmax.org/threads/will-ghk-cu-2-mg-help-with-my-hypertrophic-acne-scars.1768636/"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"GHK-Cu - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GHK-Cu"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Hair (scalp)","chain":["GHK-Cu applied to scalp","Follicle support theorised","Thicker-looking hair"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Hair-loss communities add copper peptide serums to topical stacks, aiming for thicker hair and a denser hairline. The idea draws on GHK-Cu's role in skin repair and follicle support. Research so far is in cells, animals and small facial-skin studies; no scalp hair trials were found."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["A copper peptide scalp serum is a topical cosmetic product containing GHK-Cu (copper tripeptide-1), a complex of the tripeptide glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine and copper(II), applied to the scalp with the aim of supporting hair growth or thickness.[1]","GHK-Cu occurs naturally in human plasma, saliva and urine, and was isolated from plasma by Loren Pickart in 1973.[1] It is widely used in cosmetics for anti-aging and hair-loss-prevention claims, where it is listed as copper tripeptide-1.[1] Most of the wound-healing evidence cited for GHK-Cu comes from cell cultures and animal studies, and the facial-skin studies that exist are described as small and short.[1]","No clinical studies of scalp copper peptide serums for hair loss were identified for this article."],"infobox":[["Type","Topical cosmetic peptide serum"],["Active ingredient","GHK-Cu (copper tripeptide-1)"],["Isolated","1973, from human plasma (Pickart)[1]"],["Regulatory status","Sold as a cosmetic ingredient"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["GHK-Cu is a naturally occurring tripeptide bound to copper. It is proposed to modulate wound healing, attract immune cells, act as an antioxidant and anti-inflammatory, and stimulate collagen and glycosaminoglycan synthesis in skin fibroblasts and blood vessel growth.[1] Scalp serums apply the same ingredient to the scalp, often alongside other topical hair products."],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Pickart isolated the copper-binding peptide from human plasma albumin in 1973, and in 1977 the growth-modulating peptide was identified as glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. Related work on GHK-Cu consists largely of cell-culture and animal experiments and a few small, short controlled studies on facial skin; the same source notes that GHK-Cu also increases matrix metalloproteinases, which break down dermal proteins, and that more research is needed.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Use in looksmaxxing","paras":["Copper peptide serums are discussed in hair-loss communities as an add-on to minoxidil or finasteride routines. The mechanism proposed by proponents follows the general GHK-Cu claims above (follicle support, anti-inflammatory action)."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1973","event":"Pickart isolates the copper-binding peptide from human plasma.[1]"},{"year":"1977","event":"The peptide is identified as glycyl-L-histidyl-L-lysine.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"GHK-Cu (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GHK-Cu","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"GHK-Cu (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GHK-Cu","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"GHK-Cu Microneedling Use","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-microneedling-use.1855134/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260215174337/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-microneedling-use.1855134/"},{"title":"Ghk-Cu for skin?","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-for-skin.1827238/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260202123208/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-for-skin.1827238/"},{"title":"Ghk-cu fountain","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-fountain.1820729/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260202162819/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-fountain.1820729/"},{"title":"ghk cu facial pinning","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-facial-pinning.1819870/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260305045602/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-facial-pinning.1819870/"},{"title":"ghk cu or retattutide","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-or-retattutide.1786261/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251228174753/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-or-retattutide.1786261/"},{"title":"ghk cu amino","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-amino.1777182/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20260220144101/https://looksmax.org/threads/ghk-cu-amino.1777182/"},{"title":"ghk cu t